{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he took up his parable</b> — he raised his voice so that all seventy nations would hear him, so they would be zealous for Israel. And this is 'blesses his neighbor with a loud voice' — it is reckoned to him as a curse." "<b>From Aram</b> — i.e., how do we come upon them from Aram to curse them? For from Aram Abraham their father went forth, laden with blessings, as it is stated: 'Go forth from your land' and it is written: 'And I will bless you,' etc. And so too Jacob went to Aram, laden with all those blessings, as it is stated: 'And behold I am with you and I will guard you,' etc. Another interpretation: <b>From Aram</b> — were it not for them we would not be in the world, for we are from Aram, and when Isaac was bound, Milcah too was remembered through Nahor, as it is stated: 'Behold Milcah too has borne.' And you too are ungrateful — were it not for Abraham you would not have come into the world, for through his merit Lot was saved from Sodom. And I too am ungrateful — had Jacob not come to Laban he would have had no sons. And we come from Aram to curse them!" "<b>From Aram</b> in gematria: אשל — i.e., they come by the merit of Abraham who planted an eshel." "<b>He leads me</b> — twice in the Masorah: ינחני בלק, ינחני במעגלי צדק. When that wicked man came to curse me, He led me in circles of justice without anger." "<b>He leads me</b> in gematria: לגיהנם." "<b>From the mountains of the east</b> — the mountain that the ancients established: this was a cairn and this was a cairn, and they cut a covenant upon it, as it is written: 'If I do not pass,' etc. 'this cairn,' etc. And he sent to me to transgress the covenant to curse them. Another interpretation: <b>From the mountains of the east</b> — I see that I should not curse them, for the mountains showed them honor, as it is written: 'The mountains skipped like rams' in their honor, and I would curse them?" "<b>From the mountains of the east</b> in gematria: מאבות העולם." "<b>How shall I curse Jacob, and how shall I denounce Israel</b> — He mentioned them by both their names. He said: By which name shall I curse them? The Holy One, blessed be He, blessed him when his name was Jacob, and again blessed him by the name Israel; if so, by which name shall I curse them? And the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to designate His name upon their curse, for in their curse it is written: 'And all these curses shall come upon you,' but in blessings it is written: 'YHWH will set upon you the blessing in your storehouses and in all you put your hand to' — so how shall I curse them?"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:03.761373380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}